# Two markdown files whose bytes are load-bearing, and Prettier rewrites both.
#
# The homepage hero (src/content/pages/index.md) carries a terminal transcript of
# `f help` output: column-aligned, with runs of spaces that place the uck names in
# a grid. Prettier's markdown formatter collapses those runs inside a <pre> block
# and the alignment is destroyed silently — it looked fine until the next format run.
#
# src/content/pages/examples.md quotes a blockquote from a SKILL.md whose lines
# exceed printWidth (80). Prettier cannot wrap a line that will not fit, so it
# drops the "> " continuation on the line that overflows and the quote splits into
# a blockquote plus a loose paragraph. Keeping the quote verbatim matters more than
# format-on-save for that one page.
#
# Both files are prose otherwise; a formatter that handles <pre> and long quote
# continuations can drop this list.
#
# dist/ is build output.
dist/
src/content/pages/index.md
src/content/pages/examples.md
